---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SOCIAL } from '../config/site';
import '../styles/article.css';

const updated = '13 August 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy · Team StormBreaker" description="How Team StormBreaker handles your data: we don't collect it. The details, in plain English.">
  <main>
    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <article class="article">
          <a class="back" href="/">← Back home</a>
          <header class="article-head">
            <div class="nc-meta"><span class="nc-tag">Legal</span><span class="nc-sep">/</span><span>Updated {updated}</span></div>
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
          </header>

          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              Short version: Team StormBreaker does not collect your personal data. We have no accounts,
              no analytics, and no trackers. This page explains the few technical details anyway.
            </p>

            <h2>What we collect</h2>
            <p>
              Nothing directly. <strong>stormbreaker.squadri.me</strong> is a static website. There are no
              accounts to create, no forms that send us your data, and no analytics or advertising scripts.
            </p>

            <h2>Your device</h2>
            <p>
              The only thing stored is your theme choice (light or dark), saved in your browser's local
              storage under the key <code>sb-theme</code>. It never leaves your device and we never see it.
              Clearing your browser data removes it. We do not use cookies.
            </p>

            <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
            <p>
              The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub may automatically log standard
              technical information such as your IP address and browser type when you load a page, for
              security and operational reasons. This is handled by GitHub under the GitHub Privacy Statement,
              not by us.
            </p>

            <h2>Third-party content</h2>
            <p>To keep the site fast and simple, some content loads from other services:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Fonts from Google Fonts (<code>fonts.googleapis.com</code>, <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>).</li>
              <li>Avatars and project logos from GitHub (<code>github.com</code>).</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              These providers may receive your IP address as part of delivering that content, under their
              own privacy policies.
            </p>

            <h2>Links that leave the site</h2>
            <p>
              When you click a link to download a build, donate, or join a chat, you leave our site and are
              subject to that service's own privacy policy. This includes SourceForge (downloads), PayPal
              (donations), and Telegram, Discord and X (community).
            </p>

            <h2>Children</h2>
            <p>
              StormBreaker is a general-audience project about Android kernels and is not directed at
              children under 13.
            </p>

            <h2>Changes</h2>
            <p>
              We may update this policy as the project evolves. The date at the top changes when we do.
            </p>

            <h2>Contact</h2>
            <p>
              Questions about privacy? Email us at
              <a href={`mailto:${SOCIAL.email}`}>{SOCIAL.email}</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
